  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Purchase Order Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a purchase order form?\", \"a\": \"A purchase order form is the document a buyer fills in to order goods or services from a seller. It lists what is being bought, how many and at what agreed price, under a PO number both sides can quote. Purchase order forms turn into a contract once the seller accepts the order.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a purchase order form?\", \"a\": \"Settle the fields first: both parties' details and a table of line items with the terms below it. Then describe them in one prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the form with working totals, plus a table that stores every order submitted.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free purchase order form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Template sites give away blank versions that you fill in by hand and total yourself. A free purchase order form built in Emergent prices each line and numbers each order as it arrives, and the free tier covers building and publishing it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a purchase order form template include?\", \"a\": \"Start with the PO number and order date, then the buyer's and vendor's addresses, plus a ship-to when goods go elsewhere. Each item line pairs a description and quantity with its unit price. Tax and shipping sit under the items, followed by the grand total and payment terms such as Net 30, which puts payment due 30 days after the invoice date.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a sample purchase order form look like?\", \"a\": \"A sample purchase order form reads top to bottom. The buyer's name and address sit on the left and the PO number on the right, with the vendor block below them. The item table fills the middle, and the totals and terms close the page. A work order form shares that layout but describes a job to be done.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does the buyer or the seller send purchase order forms?\", \"a\": \"The buyer fills in the PO order form and sends it to the seller. Inside a business, the person who needs the goods often files a purchase requisition first, and the PO goes out only after that request is approved. <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/purchase-order-automation'>Purchase order automation</a> handles the approvals and receiving around the form.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a purchase order form and an invoice?\", \"a\": \"They travel in opposite directions. The buyer sends a purchase order before anything ships, setting out what will be bought and at what price. The seller sends an invoice after delivery to ask for payment. Quoting the PO number on the invoice ties the two together.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do suppliers accept purchase order forms from customers?\", \"a\": \"Check the prices and delivery date against your quote. Then confirm the order to the buyer in writing, and flag any change before anything ships. Suppliers who take many customer POs can publish an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/order-form'>order form</a> that requires the buyer's PO number on every order.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I track purchase order forms after they are sent?\", \"a\": \"Give each order a status, such as confirmed or received, and change it as the order moves. A spreadsheet holds up for a handful of orders a month. With a form built in Emergent, every order is a row in a database you own, with a status column and no cap on how many orders come in.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I order paper purchase order forms?\", \"a\": \"Office supply stores sell carbonless PO books in multi-part sets, packed by the box. To order purchase order forms printed with a business name and preset numbering, ask a print shop for a custom run. A digital form needs no stock and starts numbering wherever you choose.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
